# Replit
.cache/
.local/

# --- rules restored from the pre-migration .gitignore (the migration replaced
# --- this file with a generic template and lost every repo-specific rule) ---

# The throwaway local test database (scripts/test-db.sh). A LIVE DATA
# DIRECTORY: its files change whenever the database runs, its config is
# machine-specific (the committed copy failed to even start off-Replit, locale
# errors), and it is disposable by design. Never commit it.
.pgtest/

# Database snapshots are copies of production user data. They live outside the
# repo, always.
*.sql

# Signing keys never belong in the repo. Apple's .p8 can mint client secrets
# for the Services ID for as long as the key is valid, so a committed one is a
# credential leak that no amount of later deletion undoes — git keeps it.
*.p8
*.pem
*.key
